> For either of these caches, there are techniques (checksums and the like) where we can allow the app to see whether or not it is looking at a coherent cache document or something that might not be correct.

@sftim Agreed. My question is whether we need to add such techniques to this particular cache (or caches) before we'll feel comfortable removing the fsync.

Removing the fsync from the HTTP cache would presumably bring it back down to the same level of guarantee as the discovery cache. My guess would be that the fact we were ever explicitly fsyncing each cache value in the HTTP cache was a happy accident rather than something that was explicitly a desirable quality for the HTTP cache.
